{"id": "e2049090-2c20-4dda-a5f7-9dcce6057796", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:19:15.151966", "source": "user", "parent_id": "6be68546-85c5-414b-a62c-33baaf5c8e9d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Hi — before we build anything, let's keep this to inspection and planning only (design-only task, no runs expected).\\n\\nPlease do the following:\\n1. Inspect /workspace and report what's actually there: any quantization code, clipping/ratio logic, LLAMA2-7B hooks, datasets (e.g., WikiText-2/C4), eval scripts. If the repo is empty, say so plainly.\\n2. Return a PROPOSED EXPERIMENT DESIGN for the question: effect of the runtime clipping ratio on LLAMA2-7B perplexity under symmetric input quantization + asymmetric KV-cache quantization, and the optimal fixed ratio. It must cover: rationale, clipping-ratio sweep grid (e.g., alpha in [0.90..1.00] or MAD/percentile-based variants), whether input and KV clipping are swept jointly or decoupled (I'd prefer decoupled first so we can attribute PPL changes to the right factor), bit-width assumption, eval set + sequence length + PPL definition, controls (FP16 baseline, no-clip and hard-clip extremes), and analysis plan (PPL-vs-ratio curves, sensitivity attribution, tie-breaking criteria for \\\"optimal\\\").\\n3. Feasibility notes with no-GPU / CPU-only environment in mind.\\n4. List explicit assumptions and open uncertainties — especially the bit-width, since the fixed requirements only pin down LLAMA2-7B, asymmetric KV quantization, and PPL as the metric. Don't silently choose values that change the conclusion without flagging them.\\n\\nDo NOT execute the full experiment yet. I'll review the approach first.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does the clipping ratio used during runtime quantization affect perplexity on LLAMA2-7B when applying symmetric input quantization and asymmetric KV cache quantization? What is the optimal fixed clipping ratio that balances quantization error and model accuracy in inference?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/94328/2:setup_1\", \"neurips2024/94328/2:setup_10\", \"neurips2024/94328/2:setup_17\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
